# MySettingsApp

A simple SwiftUI settings app built for my Mobile App Development course.

The app lets the user customize:

- Theme: Light / Dark Mode toggle
- Font Size: Slider-controlled text size with live preview
- Accent Color: Selectable color swatches (pink, blue, green)
- Live Preview Card: Apple-style card that updates instantly

All selections for theme and font size are saved using **UserDefaults**, so the app remembers the user’s preferences between launches.

## Tech Used

- SwiftUI (`NavigationStack`, `Form`, `Section`, `ZStack`, `VStack`, `HStack`)
- `@State` for screen-local state
- `@Binding` to update parent state from child views
- `UserDefaults` for persistent storage
- `onAppear` and `onChange` to load/save settings
